---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/system.css';

const title = 'About Pilot Protocol: Company, Team and Engineering';
const description = 'Meet the company and people behind Pilot Protocol, review our open-source and technical evidence, and learn how product content is published and corrected.';
const canonicalUrl = 'https://pilotprotocol.network/about';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <BaseHead title={title} description={description} canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    name: title,
    description,
    url: canonicalUrl,
    mainEntity: { '@id': 'https://pilotprotocol.network/#organization' },
  })}></script>
</head>
<body>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <section class="about-hero">
      <div class="gridbg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="wrap about-hero-grid">
        <div><span class="about-eyebrow">About Pilot Protocol</span><h1>Building the network<br/><em>agents can use.</em></h1></div>
        <div class="about-intro"><p>Pilot Protocol develops an open-source network layer for software agents: persistent identity and addressing, encrypted peer connectivity, explicit trust, discovery, and installable agent-facing capabilities.</p><p>The service and website are operated by <strong>Vulture Labs, Inc.</strong>, a Delaware corporation.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-facts" aria-labelledby="company-facts">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="about-head"><span class="about-eyebrow">Company facts</span><h2 id="company-facts">A public trail from<br/><em>claim to evidence.</em></h2></div>
        <div class="facts-grid">
          <article><span>Product</span><h3>Pilot Protocol</h3><p>Agent networking software, a shared backbone, managed-network capabilities, and an app ecosystem.</p><a href="/learn/what-is-pilot-protocol">Product overview →</a></article>
          <article><span>Operator</span><h3>Vulture Labs, Inc.</h3><p>The legal operator identified in the site’s terms, privacy policy, and publisher agreement.</p><a href="/terms">Terms of service →</a></article>
          <article><span>Source</span><h3>Open core</h3><p>The daemon source, releases, issue history, and license are available for technical inspection.</p><a href="https://github.com/pilot-protocol/pilotprotocol" rel="noopener">Review the repository ↗</a></article>
          <article><span>Contact</span><h3>Direct to the team</h3><p>Enterprise, partnership, press, correction, and security paths reach the people operating Pilot.</p><a href="/contact">Contact Pilot Protocol →</a></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-people" aria-labelledby="people">
      <div class="wrap people-grid">
        <div><span class="about-eyebrow">People and authorship</span><h2 id="people">Put a name behind<br/><em>the work.</em></h2></div>
        <div class="people-list">
          <article><span>Leadership</span><h3>Razvan Roman</h3><p>Co-founder and CEO. Author of the company’s July 2026 launch and financing announcement.</p><a href="/news/pilot-raises-4-5m-seed">Read the announcement →</a></article>
          <article><span>Technical authorship</span><h3>Teodor-Ioan Calin</h3><p>Named author on Pilot Protocol technical papers and specifications collected in the research documentation.</p><a href="/docs/research">Review technical papers →</a></article>
          <article><span>Product publishing</span><h3>Pilot Protocol editorial team</h3><p>Documentation and product articles are published under the organization when no individual byline is assigned.</p><a href="#publishing">Read the publishing standard ↓</a></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-publishing" id="publishing" aria-labelledby="publishing-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="about-head"><span class="about-eyebrow">Publishing standard</span><h2 id="publishing-title">Who, how,<br/><em>and why.</em></h2></div>
        <div class="publishing-grid">
          <article><span>01</span><h3>Who created it</h3><p>Articles identify an individual author when one is known and otherwise name the Pilot Protocol editorial team. Technical papers retain their named authors.</p></article>
          <article><span>02</span><h3>How claims are scoped</h3><p>Product content should distinguish currently available behavior from early-access capabilities and roadmap direction. Version-specific commands belong in documentation; architecture and evidence belong in technical references.</p></article>
          <article><span>03</span><h3>Why we publish</h3><p>The goal is to help builders and evaluators decide whether Pilot fits a deployment—not to blur connectivity, application authorization, governance, and business authority into one promise.</p></article>
          <article><span>04</span><h3>How corrections work</h3><p>Readers can report a factual or technical issue through the contact path. Security-sensitive reports use the separate disclosure channel. Material edits should update the visible page date.</p></article>
        </div>
        <div class="evidence-row">
          <a href="/trust"><span>Security and architecture</span><b>Trust Center</b><i>→</i></a>
          <a href="/governance"><span>Authority and control</span><b>Governance model</b><i>→</i></a>
          <a href="/roadmap"><span>Available, next, later</span><b>Product roadmap</b><i>→</i></a>
          <a href="/security/disclosure"><span>Responsible reporting</span><b>Security disclosure</b><i>→</i></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />

  <style>
    .about-eyebrow { display: block; margin-bottom: 24px; color: var(--ink-dim); font: 560 10px/1 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .15em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .about-hero { position: relative; overflow: hidden; padding: 104px 0 88px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .about-hero-grid, .people-grid { position: relative; z-index: 1; display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(300px, .9fr); gap: 72px; align-items: end; }
    .about-hero h1, .about-head h2, .people-grid h2 { margin: 0; font-weight: 500; line-height: .92; letter-spacing: -.052em; }
    .about-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(58px, 8.5vw, 132px); }
    h1 em, h2 em { color: var(--accent-text); font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; }
    .about-intro { display: grid; gap: 22px; }
    .about-intro p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: clamp(17px, 1.7vw, 22px); line-height: 1.5; }
    .about-intro strong { color: var(--ink); }
    .about-facts, .about-people, .about-publishing { padding: 104px 0; }
    .about-people { border-block: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-2); }
    .about-head { margin-bottom: 52px; }
    .about-head h2, .people-grid h2 { font-size: clamp(46px, 6vw, 82px); }
    .facts-grid, .publishing-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .facts-grid article, .publishing-grid article { display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 310px; padding: 28px; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .facts-grid article > span, .publishing-grid article > span, .people-list article > span, .evidence-row span { color: var(--accent-text); font: 530 9px/1 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
    .facts-grid h3, .publishing-grid h3 { margin: 68px 0 12px; font-size: 24px; letter-spacing: -.025em; }
    .facts-grid p, .publishing-grid p, .people-list p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; }
    .facts-grid a { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 24px; color: var(--accent-text); font: 520 10px/1 var(--mono); text-transform: uppercase; }
    .people-grid { align-items: start; }
    .people-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--line-2); }
    .people-list article { padding: 28px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2); }
    .people-list h3 { margin: 14px 0 10px; font-size: 28px; }
    .people-list a { display: inline-block; margin-top: 16px; color: var(--accent-text); font: 520 10px/1 var(--mono); text-transform: uppercase; }
    .evidence-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); margin-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .evidence-row a { display: grid; gap: 12px; padding: 24px; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); color: inherit; }
    .evidence-row b { font-size: 16px; }
    .evidence-row i { color: var(--accent-text); font-style: normal; }
    @media (max-width: 980px) {
      .facts-grid, .publishing-grid, .evidence-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
      .about-hero-grid, .people-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 42px; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 620px) {
      .about-hero { padding: 70px 0 58px; }
      .about-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(48px, 14vw, 72px); }
      .about-facts, .about-people, .about-publishing { padding: 72px 0; }
      .facts-grid, .publishing-grid, .evidence-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .facts-grid article, .publishing-grid article { min-height: 250px; }
      .facts-grid h3, .publishing-grid h3 { margin-top: 48px; }
    }
  </style>
</body>
</html>
